// 002.9 (D17): One unified contextual grammar accepts Charter's single-word uppercase
// words as unquoted atoms AND `tick` as an Event/Act identifier, alongside Charter
// declarations (`Param`, `Immunity`, `Held(...) For ...`, `Scenario`) with no `--eflint` flag.
Fact label Identified by Valid, Except, Due, Immunity, Against, Unless, Scenario, Document, Clause, Approved, Text, Norm, From, Module, Use, As, Param, Held.
Fact party Identified by Alice.
Param wait-time : Duration = 2.
Fact stamp Identified by party.
Act mark Actor party Holds when True Creates stamp(party).
Act revoke-mark Actor party Recipient party Holds when Held(stamp(party)) For wait-time Terminates stamp(party).
Immunity protect-mark Holder party Against revoke-mark Holds when label(Against) Unless label(Unless).

+label(Valid).
+label(Text).
+label(From).
+label(Against).
+label(Held).
?label(Valid).
?label(Text).
?label(From).
?label == Valid || label == Text || label == From || label == Against || label == Held.

mark(Alice).
@ 2.
?!valid revoke-mark(Alice, Alice).

Scenario event-tick-and-atoms {
  Event tick Creates label(Scenario).
  tick().
  ?label(Scenario).
  -label(Scenario).
  tick.
  ?label(Scenario).
}
